{
  "_readme": [
    "US-2843 AC2. Labelled listing photo sets for the stock-photo detector gate.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. These are hand-authored METADATA sets, not",
    "images sampled from live eBay listings, because the calibration spike",
    "(US-2842) that would give us real ones cannot run without production",
    "credentials. So this fixture proves the predicate behaves as specified. It",
    "does NOT prove the tells generalise to the real marketplace. Replace these",
    "with sampled real sets when US-2842 runs, and re-record the baselines in",
    "comp-stock-photo_test.ts against whatever they then measure.",
    "",
    "TWO CASES ARE KEPT BECAUSE THEY FAIL. S15 is a catalog set the detector",
    "misses, and E15 is a seller set it wrongly flags. Deleting them would lift",
    "the scores and teach the next reader nothing. They are the honest edges of",
    "what metadata alone can decide.",
    "",
    "hashCellCounts maps a photo hash to the number of DISTINCT cells it has been",
    "seen under. Anything absent counts as one."
  ],
